It is the lunch break.
I need a SIM card for my phone.
I go into a mobile phone shop.
A shop assistant comes.
"Good afternoon," he says.
"Are you looking for something?"
"Good afternoon," I answer.
"I need a German SIM card."
The assistant nods.
"Do you have your passport?" he asks.
"Yes," I say.
"Here is my passport."
He takes the passport.
"You also need an address in Germany," he says.
"Do you have a registration?"
"Yes, I have the paper," I say.
I open my backpack.
"Here is the registration."
"Perfect," the assistant says.
